    "lyrics": [],
    "notes": "Two parts (Viola, Violoncello), one staff each, 20 bars of 3/4 in F major.  Viola: alto clef, treble from bar 13 (at a line break: courtesy clef at the end of system 3) back to alto before beat 3 of bar 17.  Cello: bass -> tenor at bar 5 (line start, courtesy clef at end of system 1) -> treble before beat 2 of bar 6 -> tenor at bar 9 (line start) -> bass at bar 11 -> tenor before beat 2 of bar 17 -> bass at bar 19.  Small mid-bar clefs change the pitch of every following note; a correct conversion places each <clef> change at the exact beat and keeps all pitches (e.g. cello bar 6: G4 in tenor clef then Bb4, D5 in treble clef).  Courtesy clefs at system ends are not clef changes of the following bar content beyond what is listed."
  },
